  "title": "Coast Guard Rescue Mission",
  "description": "B-roll of a Coast Guard air crew rescuing a fatigued, trans-Atlantic rower about 150 miles east of Cape Cod, Mass. Charlie Girard, 28, from France, called the Coast Guard around 8:25 a.m., using a satellite phone and activated his Emergency Position Indicating Radio Beacon, to help the Coast Guard to find his position. Coast Guard Air Station Cape Cod launched a Falcon jet and a Jayhawk helicopter rescue crew to hoist Girard from his 21-foot row boat and return him to shore.",
